"""Explanatory diagrams for the paper (vector PDFs in figures/), regenerated by `make.py diagrams`.

One style for all: the Okabe–Ito colour-blind-safe palette, with hatching or line style as a second
cue so each figure reads in greyscale; thin lines; every element labelled; no decoration. The 3-D
panels are painted by lighting.py (key and fill light, ambient occlusion, and the true body's edges
as fine dots sorted in depth with the voxels), shared with octree_diagrams.py.

    a  diag-representations.pdf   a triangle (2-D) and a square-based pyramid (3-D): true surface,
                                  staircase voxels, interior cells + clipped boundary pieces
    b  diag-fill-moments.pdf      fill fraction, centroid against cell centre, second moment
    c  diag-cuts.pdf              one cell cut by planes: the clipped piece in each case
    d  diag-closed-form.pdf       one face and one edge as the closed form sees them
    (e, the layered read, is drawn with the octree figures in octree_diagrams.py)

Words as the paper uses them: "exact" is the analytic shape; a clipped piece is exact *to the mesh*.

    python scripts/diagrams.py
"""

